e private link it shares with node1) on TCP port 80 of node1's management address (10.100.201.10). node3 reaches it there and gets HTTP 200; all other sources are refused. Verified persistence across a one-at-a-time restart of all three nodes.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered node1 is OPNsense/FreeBSD (mgmt LAN vtnet0=10.100.201.10, unconfigured vtnet1); node2/node3 are AlmaLinux 9 on shared 10.100.201.0/24; node2 has a second unconfigured NIC eth1 shared only with node1\",\"Created and enabled a systemd HTTP service (python3 http.server) on node2:8080 serving /srv/www, since none was running yet\",\"Configured a private point-to-point link: node1 opt1/vtnet1=10.50.50.1/24 (OPNsense config.xml + configctl interface reconfigure opt1), node2 eth1=10.50.50.2/24 (nmcli, persistent)\",\"Added a persistent host route on node2 (10.100.201.12/32 via 10.50.50.1 dev eth1) so replies to node3 return via node1 instead of node2's directly-connected eth0, avoiding asymmetric routing\",\"Restricted node2 firewalld so port 8080 is open only on eth1 (new 'priv' zone), not on shared eth0, so node2's service isn't directly reachable from node3\",\"Edited node1 /conf/config.xml: added NAT port-forward rule (lan mgmt:80 -> 10.50.50.2:8080) and an associated pf pass rule restricted to source 10.100.201.12 (node3) only; applied via configctl filter reload\",\"Found and disabled OPNsense's automatic HTTP->HTTPS anti-lockout rule (webgui/disablehttpredirect) which had been allowing any source to port 80, defeating the restriction\",\"Verified node3 gets 200/hello-from-node2 on http://10.100.201.10:80/, while node2 and a direct probe to node2:8080 both fail/timeout\",\"Captured pre-restart boot markers and health (kern.boottime on node1, boot_id on node2/node3, service/route/NAT/filter state) on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via configctl system reboot, node2 and node3 via systemctl reboot, one at a time, polling until each came back\",\"Confirmed changed boot identity on all three nodes post-restart and re-verified interface addressing, routes, firewalld zone, NAT/filter rules, and end-to-end HTTP reachability/refusal after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 has an HTTP service reachable on 8080 on the network shared with node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a16a37f9ccd74195\",\"cmd-2b76c49fa23d4e5b\",\"cmd-a442e38729534f04\",\"cmd-82c7c9545a534bc0\"],\"summary\":\"Created/enabled simplehttp.service on node2:8080; confirmed listening and reachable from node1 over the new private link 10.50.50.0/24\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2's service is not directly reachable from node3 over the shared management network\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5fafc3dabea04afc\",\"cmd-033464644d0f4ac2\"],\"summary\":\"firewalld on node2 only opens 8080 on eth1 (priv zone); curl from node3 to 10.100.201.11:8080 timed out (exit 28)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service published on TCP port 80 of node1's management address, reachable by node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-072990481e8e48f7\",\"cmd-f12a31fd0693423c\",\"cmd-11670c2ed73a4342\",\"cmd-f0c0e23b1d4349ef\"],\"summary\":\"Added NAT rdr rule (lan:80 -> 10.50.50.2:8080) in config.xml, reloaded pf, confirmed rdr rule active and node3 gets HTTP 200 'hello-from-node2' from http://10.100.201.10:80/\"},{\"requirement\":\"Published port refused for every other source address\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c8a481a36ee24980\",\"cmd-271a7e37167747e3\",\"cmd-a69aaf20a22a4c9e\",\"cmd-b88a36d2efda4c33\",\"cmd-9989d702f1294585\"],\"summary\":\"Found and neutralized the OPNsense anti-lockout rule that allowed any source to port 80 (disablehttpredirect); final pf ruleset shows only source 10.100.201.12 (node3) is passed to port 80; curl from node2 to 10.100.201.10:80 times out both before and after node restarts\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-47994a37b1ca47b3\",\"cmd-9a790529f9524d8f\",\"cmd-b4362d1d6b0f4095\",\"cmd-4da7468e3c5e4ba8\",\"cmd-0a482c002ca04e83\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime/NAT/filter/service captured; configctl system reboot acknowledged then connection dropped; kern.boottime changed (16:24:15->16:32:28); post-reboot opt1 IP, NAT rule, restricted filter rule, and node3's HTTP 200 all recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-75219643fba54b08\",\"cmd-419d8c1271d74fc7\",\"cmd-0f41f7aa584d4f7c\",\"cmd-b03d6df570404e65\",\"cmd-365b825d90574a05\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id/service/eth1/route captured; systemctl reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed (c2ffc729->70ac69c1); post-reboot service active, eth1 IP, route, firewalld priv zone, and node3's HTTP 200 all recovered\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ddfba354e9604490\",\"cmd-200ca59fe5c54c11\",\"cmd-bd44392ff3d04753\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id and working curl to published service captured; systemctl reboot acknowledged; boot_id changed (a0d04bc6->b9a0d769); post-reboot curl to http://10.100.201.10:80/ still returns 200 'hello-from-node2'\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Published node2's HTTP service (port 8080, on the private link it shares with node1) on TCP port 80 of node1's management address (10.100.201.10). node3 reaches it there and gets HTTP 200; all other sources are refused. Verified persistence across a one-at-a-time restart of all three nodes.","actions_performed":["Discovered node1 is OPNsense/FreeBSD (mgmt LAN vtnet0=10.100.201.10, unconfigured vtnet1); node2/node3 are AlmaLinux 9 on shared 10.100.201.0/24; node2 has a second unconfigured NIC eth1 shared only with node1","Created and enabled a systemd HTTP service (python3 http.server) on node2:8080 serving /srv/www, since none was running yet","Configured a private point-to-point link: node1 opt1/vtnet1=10.50.50.1/24 (OPNsense config.xml + configctl interface reconfigure opt1), node2 eth1=10.50.50.2/24 (nmcli, persistent)","Added a persistent host route on node2 (10.100.201.12/32 via 10.50.50.1 dev eth1) so replies to node3 return via node1 instead of node2's directly-connected eth0, avoiding asymmetric routing","Restricted node2 firewalld so port 8080 is open only on eth1 (new 'priv' zone), not on shared eth0, so node2's service isn't directly reachable from node3","Edited node1 /conf/config.xml: added NAT port-forward rule (lan mgmt:80 -> 10.50.50.2:8080) and an associated pf pass rule restricted to source 10.100.201.12 (node3) only; applied via configctl filter reload","Found and disabled OPNsense's automatic HTTP->HTTPS anti-lockout rule (webgui/disablehttpredirect) which had been allowing any source to port 80, defeating the restriction","Verified node3 gets 200/hello-from-node2 on http://10.100.201.10:80/, while node2 and a direct probe to node2:8080 both fail/timeout","Captured pre-restart boot markers and health (kern.boottime on node1, boot_id on node2/node3, service/route/NAT/filter state) on all three nodes","Restarted node1 via configctl system reboot, node2 and node3 via systemctl reboot, one at a time, polling until each came back","Confirmed changed boot identity on all three nodes post-restart and re-verified interface addressing, routes, firewalld zone, NAT/filter rules, and end-to-end HTTP reachability/refusal after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node2 has an HTTP service reachable on 8080 on the network shared with node1","command_ids":["cmd-a16a37f9ccd74195","cmd-2b76c49fa23d4e5b","cmd-a442e38729534f04","cmd-82c7c9545a534bc0"],"summary":"Created/enabled simplehttp.service on node2:8080; confirmed listening and reachable from node1 over the new private link 10.50.50.0/24"},{"requirement":"node2's service is not directly reachable from node3 over the shared management network","command_ids":["cmd-5fafc3dabea04afc","cmd-033464644d0f4ac2"],"summary":"firewalld on nod